The top of the table is dominated by institutions whose Academic Reputation scores sit in the high 90s. Among the top 10, two programs have Academic Reputation scores above 98, and their Employer Reputation scores range from 95.8 to 100. The Citations scores among the top group show more variation, with some institutions scoring in the 80s while others reach the low 90s. This suggests that research output and citation impact are not the sole determinants of the highest ranks — reputation among academics and employers carries substantial weight in this subject.

