The US leads with 41, but the distribution within the top 100 is even more telling. The United States contributes 41 institutions to the full 201-program list, the largest count of any country or region. The United Kingdom contributes 22 institutions and China (Mainland) contributes 13 to the full 201-program list. Australia contributes 13 institutions to the full 201-program list. India and Spain each contribute 8 institutions to the full 201-program list.

## Why no median rank is published

A median rank cannot be computed for this list, because the institution at the median position has only a published rank range (101-200) rather than an exact rank. This is a useful reference point: the institution at the median position has only a published rank range (101-200), so no median rank can be computed for the 201 ranked programs. But the median also highlights how quickly the field is expanding — QS publishes a rank band of 101-200 for 101 institutions, and QS publishes an overall score for only 50 of the 201 ranked programs, so no score comparison is possible for the remaining 151, which are still ranked.

## Data notes

This analysis is based on the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026 for Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, published by Quacquarelli Symonds (QS), with a data reference date of April 3, 2026. The ranking covers 60 subject tables in total; this article uses only the Data Science and Artificial Intelligence table. The global list includes 201 institutions across 37 countries and regions.

The ranking methodology incorporates Academic Reputation, Employer Reputation, Citations per paper, H-index, and International Research Network scores. The scores shown in the table are the overall scores that determine rank order. Ranks are assigned as the lower-bound integer of the computed position; ties are resolved by the ranking algorithm and are not broken by score alone.

The country leaderboard counts each institution once, based on the country or region listed in the ranking data. Institutions with multiple campuses or joint programs are counted under their primary country of affiliation. A median rank cannot be computed for the ordered list of 201 institutions, because the institution at the median position has only a published rank range (101-200); it does not represent an average score or a threshold for inclusion in any particular tier.

The rank bands and score bands presented here are derived from the published ranking data and reflect the distribution as of the April 3, 2026 data cut. No projections or estimates are made beyond the published figures.
